From 075df19a6c9abdb9b2c04e52dadb10ccf945941d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:00:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 36/37] VideoOutput: the imported frames' textures are made
 readable by the passes, and an import that reads as zeros is refused and said

First run on the A10 (a real VA-API frame, Carrizo decoding, Carrizo and Hainan drawing): the import was reported "imported" and the views
were drawn from all-zero planes (a green picture). Qt's VA-API converter binds the DMA-BUF's EGLImage to a texture it generated and leaves the
filters as created (a minification filter that needs mipmaps: the texture is incomplete), because the scene graph's sampler sets them when it
draws; the passes here read the level 0 by texel, and an incomplete texture reads as zeros. The planes' filters are now set to nearest before the
passes read them, and the first frames of a stream (and every sixtieth) are sampled at the middle of the picture: luma and chroma all zero
is no picture, so the import is refused, the frames are copied from then on and lastFrameRouteWhy() says why (a DMA-BUF another GPU accepts and
reads as zeros is no import). VideoOutput.stereoDepthReadBacks() counts the checks and the empty ones.

Tests: depthImportsHardwareFrames' double now leaves the filters as the converter does (red without the fix: the views come out of zeros),
depthRefusesEmptyImportedPlanes (all-zero planes are copied and said; red without the check), depthTextureFramesConvertLikeTheCopies (a consumer
on another thread gets from a frame of textures what it gets from the read back frame, 8, 10 and 16 bits).

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
